1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,400
 I don't pretend to know how it works, but it feels like a sort of divine mending

2
00:00:04,400 --> 00:00:08,080
 that changes what's happening to you into something happening for you.

3
00:00:08,720 --> 00:00:13,440
 Let me leave this last visual image from a sculpting class my brother can't took in college.

4
00:00:13,440 --> 00:00:17,840
 He said, "Our final assignment was to sculpt a bust of ourselves out of clay.

5
00:00:17,840 --> 00:00:20,080
 I thought to myself, this is going to be easy enough."

6
00:00:20,640 --> 00:00:23,200
 We began and I realized it wasn't easy at all.

7
00:00:23,760 --> 00:00:26,560
 When I looked at the piece, the eyes were terrible.

8
00:00:26,560 --> 00:00:30,400
 no matter how hard I tried, I couldn't get the eyes to look lifelike.

9
00:00:30,400 --> 00:00:34,240
 I observed my classmates and noticed our instructor was helping them.

10
00:00:34,240 --> 00:00:38,080
 He was very good. I, however, didn't want help.

11
00:00:38,080 --> 00:00:42,240
 I wanted this to be my piece. I struggled alone for quite a while

12
00:00:42,240 --> 00:00:45,120
 until I finally humbled myself and asked for help.

13
00:00:45,120 --> 00:00:48,320
 The instructor came over and deftly started carving.

14
00:00:48,320 --> 00:00:51,840
 He did it so aggressively and abruptly that it startled me.

15
00:00:51,840 --> 00:00:54,640
 He dug into the clay much further than I had,

16
00:00:54,640 --> 00:00:57,760
 And within a few minutes, the eyes came to life.

17
00:00:57,760 --> 00:01:00,740
 It looked so good, there was no way I could have done it.

18
00:01:00,740 --> 00:01:02,800
 As I stepped back and looked at the piece,

19
00:01:02,800 --> 00:01:05,120
 I could see that it was uniquely me.

20
00:01:05,120 --> 00:01:07,420
 And yet, without a doubt, a master's hand

21
00:01:07,420 --> 00:01:09,720
 had shaped what mine could not.

22
00:01:09,720 --> 00:01:12,340
 My friends, there is a sculpting taking place

23
00:01:12,340 --> 00:01:15,000
 within each of our souls to invite the Savior

24
00:01:15,000 --> 00:01:16,760
 to become involved as hard.

25
00:01:16,760 --> 00:01:18,560
 Our pride gets in the way.

26
00:01:18,560 --> 00:01:20,600
 He'll lovingly chasten us to get our attention,

27
00:01:20,600 --> 00:01:24,560
 but waits for an invitation before he can really go to work.

28
00:01:24,560 --> 00:01:28,240
 Then He will start carving, sometimes surprising us with how

29
00:01:28,240 --> 00:01:30,720
 abrupt and aggressive the work feels.

30
00:01:30,720 --> 00:01:34,760
 But as time goes on, we'll begin to see the work of His hand.

31
00:01:34,760 --> 00:01:39,000
 God is shaping us into something only He knows we can become.

32
00:01:39,000 --> 00:01:41,680
 And one day, when all of the suffering and loneliness

